---
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/Base.astro";

const meta = {
	description:
		"About this fan transcription of Running Around Portland (1979) — the book, this project, and its copyright status.",
	title: "About",
};
---

<PageLayout meta={meta}>
	<h1 class="title mb-12">About</h1>
	<div class="prose lg:prose-lg prose-cactus">
		<p>
			<em>Running Around Portland</em> is a long out-of-print 1979 guidebook by John Perry and Buzz
			Willits, with photography by Ancil Nance, published by Running Around Portland Press. It describes 44 running
			routes around Portland, Vancouver, and the surrounding hills — grouped into five sections,
			each with a hand-drawn course map, a difficulty and conditions rating, a beginning point,
			and a turn-by-turn narrative in the authors' own voice.
		</p>
		<p>
			This site is a fan-made, non-commercial transcription of that book. Each route gets its own
			page with the original map, any accompanying photo, and the route's text copied out
			verbatim (typos and all) from the scanned original. The <a class="cactus-link" href="/">home page</a> lists all of them grouped by section, with distance and difficulty at a glance and a map
			showing roughly where each one starts.
		</p>
		<p>Also transcribed from the book's back matter:</p>
		<ul class="list-inside list-disc" role="list">
			<li><a class="cactus-link" href="/appendix/running-organizations/">Running organizations and publications</a> active in 1979</li>
			<li><a class="cactus-link" href="/appendix/annual-runs-calendar/">A calendar of annual organized runs</a> around Portland and Vancouver</li>
			<li><a class="cactus-link" href="/appendix/calorie-table/">A calorie table</a> and <a class="cactus-link" href="/appendix/aerobic-point-tables/">aerobic point tables</a> for walking and running</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			A couple of things are still incomplete: two routes (Ester Short Park Run and Lacamas Lake
			Loop) came out too blurred in the original scans to transcribe, and a few months are missing
			from the annual-runs calendar for the same reason. Both are noted where they're missing,
			pending better scans of the original book.
		</p>
		<h2>Copyright</h2>
		<p>
			Text and maps &copy; 1979 the original authors and Running Around Portland Press. All rights remain with them;
			nothing here is claimed as original work, and nothing on this site is for sale. It exists
			because the book is long out of print and hard to find, and because these are still good
			routes.
		</p>
		<p>
			The source and transcription scripts are on <a class="cactus-link" href="https://github.com/lbeckman314/running-around-portland" rel="noreferrer" target="_blank">GitHub</a>.
		</p>
	</div>
</PageLayout>
